# R&C Roofing — AI Agent Context

This is the **R&C Roofing Contractors** website built on Astro v7 + Tailwind CSS v4 (AstroWind template).

## Read These Files First

Before writing or editing any page, always read:
- `PAGE-BUILDER.md` — pattern library (P-01 to P-13), pattern selector, global rules, typography classes, and the new page checklist
- `TEMPLATE-GUIDE.md` — full design system reference, component API, and site architecture

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- Every page lives at `src/pages/[route]/index.astro`
- Max content width: `max-w-[1400px] mx-auto` on every `WidgetWrapper`
- Backgrounds alternate white → grey → white → grey down the page
- No eyebrow/tagline text above headings
- Simple heading+description cards (no link/button) always get a Tabler icon mark via `InfoCard`. Do not add icons to P-05 service cards that already have a bottom link
- Only use typography classes defined in `PAGE-BUILDER.md` — never invent new sizes
- Heading + paragraph(s) + CTA is always P-03 with a side image. Flip the image side from the previous split on the page (Hero2 is image-right, so the next split is image-left / `isReversed`)
- Grid cards with a link or button: card is `flex flex-col h-full`, body is `flex-1`, CTA is `mt-auto` so links line up at the bottom regardless of copy length
- Adjacent sections must use different structures — never two card grids in a row
- Never lay out 5 items as cards (no 3+2). Use P-06 `IconPointBand` (horizontal icon points), or a `ServiceDirectory` for linked items
- H2 + 3 or 5 icon points (no links): `IconPointBand` — one row, icon above title, left-aligned. Not a timeline, not cards
- H2 + 4 unlinked icon points as text (no cards): `IconPointGrid` — 2 × 2, icon above title, left-aligned
- Yellow / accent-tint cards (`bg-card-light`, `bg-accent`, yellow wash) — including those on grey `#FAFAFA`: links use `text-heading` (`#222`) or `text-card-link-light`. Never `text-primary` or `text-accent` — those blend into the yellow
- Run `npm run build` after every page change and fix any errors before finishing

## Hero Rules

- Omit `actions` and `<Fragment slot="content">` from `Hero2` on content-heavy or informational pages (Our Story, Reviews, Gallery, etc.)
- Only include CTA + badges on conversion-focused heroes (service pages, homepage)
- To add a visual subheading between H1 and body copy inside `Hero2`, use a styled `<span class="block text-[20px] md:text-[24px] font-medium font-heading text-heading mb-6 leading-[130%] tracking-tight">` as the first element inside `<Fragment slot="subtitle">`

## Pattern Quick Reference

| Shape | Pattern |
|---|---|
| H1 + paragraphs + optional CTA + image + badges | P-01 |
| H2 + intro paragraphs + 2–4 item columns | P-02 |
| H2 + paragraphs + image one side + optional CTA | P-03 |
| H2 title sharing a row with a CTA button | P-04 |
| 4–6 cards with per-card links | P-05 |
| 3 or 5 icon points, no cards (one horizontal row) | P-06 |
| 4 icon + heading + description, 2 × 2 text grid, no cards | P-14 |
| 4 compact info cards one row | P-07 |
| H2 + steps/timeline + optional image | P-08 |
| Grid of project/gallery cards | P-09 |
| FAQ accordion | P-10 |
| Testimonials/reviews | P-11 |
| Page-ending CTA card (every page) | P-12 |
| H2 + multiple paragraphs, full width, no image/columns — narrative sections | P-13 |

## Updating PAGE-BUILDER.md

When a new layout is approved in the browser, add it to `PAGE-BUILDER.md`:
1. Add a row to the Pattern Selector table
2. Add a full `### P-XX · Name` entry with snippet and variants
3. Update the next available number note at the bottom of the table
